classDiagram
    direction LR

    class ClassSession {
        <<external — scheduling>>
    }
    class AcademicActor {
        <<external — academic>>
    }
    class School {
        <<external — academic>>
    }
    class Cohort {
        <<external — academic>>
    }
    class Person {
        <<external — identity>>
    }
    class AppUser {
        <<external — identity>>
    }

    class AttendanceRecord {
        +Long attendanceRecordId
        +Long classSessionId
        +Long academicActorId
        +AttendanceStatus attendanceStatus
        +DateTime capturedAt
        +CaptureMethod captureMethod
        +Decimal matchScore
        +record()
    }

    class AttendanceStatus {
        <<enumeration>>
        Present
        Absent
        Late
        Justified
    }

    class CaptureMethod {
        <<enumeration>>
        FACIAL
        MANUAL
        IOT
        IMPORT
    }

    class JustificationType {
        +Int justificationTypeId
        +Int schoolId
        +String name
        +String description
        +Boolean requiresAttachment
        +Boolean status
    }

    class Justification {
        +Long justificationId
        +Long attendanceRecordId
        +Int justificationTypeId
        +String reason
        +DateTime submittedAt
        +UUID reviewedBy
        +DateTime reviewedAt
        +ReviewStatus reviewStatus
        +String resolutionNotes
        +submit()
        +review(decision)
    }

    class ReviewStatus {
        <<enumeration>>
        Pending
        Approved
        Rejected
    }

    class SupportingDocument {
        +Long supportingDocumentId
        +Long justificationId
        +String fileName
        +String storageUri
        +String mimeType
        +Long sizeBytes
        +upload()
    }

    class AttendanceReport {
        <<derived projection, no FKs>>
        +UUID reportId
        +Int schoolId
        +Long cohortId
        +UUID generatedBy
        +String reportType
        +JSON filters
        +JSON result
        +DateTime generatedAt
    }

    class BiometricUpdateCase {
        +UUID caseId
        +UUID personId
        +BiometricType biometricType
        +Int fingerNumber
        +String currentEmbeddingRef
        +String reason
        +UpdateStatus updateStatus
        +UUID requestedBy
        +DateTime requestedAt
        +UUID reviewedBy
        +DateTime reviewedAt
        +String resolutionNotes
        +request()
        +review(decision)
    }

    class BiometricType {
        <<enumeration>>
        FACIAL
        FINGERPRINT
    }

    class UpdateStatus {
        <<enumeration>>
        Pending
        In_Review
        Approved
        Rejected
    }

    class FacialEmbedding {
        <<MongoDB document>>
        +ObjectId _id
        +UUID personId
        +Int templateVersion
        +Float[] encoding
        +String modelVersion
        +DateTime enrolledAt
        +Boolean isActive
        +enroll()
        +deactivate()
    }

    class FingerprintEmbedding {
        <<MongoDB document>>
        +ObjectId _id
        +UUID personId
        +Int fingerNumber
        +Int templateVersion
        +Float[] encoding
        +String modelVersion
        +DateTime enrolledAt
        +Boolean isActive
        +enroll()
        +deactivate()
    }

    AttendanceRecord "1" --> "0..1" Justification : justification.attendance_record_id FK — unique one-to-one
    JustificationType "1" --> "0..*" Justification : justification.justification_type_id FK
    Justification "1" --> "0..*" SupportingDocument : supporting_document.justification_id FK
    AttendanceRecord --> AttendanceStatus
    AttendanceRecord --> CaptureMethod
    Justification --> ReviewStatus
    BiometricUpdateCase --> BiometricType
    BiometricUpdateCase --> UpdateStatus

    AttendanceRecord ..> ClassSession : class_session_id — cross-context, no FK
    AttendanceRecord ..> AcademicActor : academic_actor_id — cross-context, no FK
    Justification ..> AppUser : reviewed_by — cross-context, no FK
    AttendanceReport ..> School : school_id — no FK (derived projection)
    AttendanceReport ..> Cohort : cohort_id — no FK (derived projection)
    AttendanceReport ..> AppUser : generated_by — no FK (derived projection)
    BiometricUpdateCase ..> Person : person_id — cross-context, no FK
    BiometricUpdateCase ..> AppUser : requested_by / reviewed_by — cross-context, no FK
    BiometricUpdateCase ..> FacialEmbedding : current_embedding_ref — cross-paradigm (Mongo _id), no FK
    BiometricUpdateCase ..> FingerprintEmbedding : current_embedding_ref — cross-paradigm (Mongo _id), no FK
    FacialEmbedding ..> Person : person_id — cross-context, no FK
    FingerprintEmbedding ..> Person : person_id — cross-context, no FK

    note for AttendanceRecord "RN-22: one record per academic_actor per class_session (uq_attendance_session_actor). RN-23: the session must be Open when recorded. Only captureMethod=MANUAL is wired for the alternative path (RN-26) — FACIAL capture is designed but no client calls the write yet, see SEQ-01."
    note for JustificationType "school_id NULL = global type. uq_justification_type_school_name plus a partial unique on name WHERE school_id IS NULL."
    note for Justification "RN-32: exactly one justification per attendance_record (1:1, UNIQUE). RN-33 (intended): requires_attachment should block approval without a document — not enforced server-side today. RN-36 (intended): approval should cascade attendance_status to Justified — it does not (see ST-02 / SEQ-03)."
    note for SupportingDocument "Designed but not wired: no client ever calls this endpoint with a real file, see SEQ-03."
    note for BiometricUpdateCase "Logically owned by Biometric, physically hosted in the configuration schema (transient, see AGENTS.md §4.6). chk_finger_number: 1..10 only if biometricType=FINGERPRINT, else NULL. requestedBy/requestedAt are mandatory. This is the canonical shape — ms-biometric also runs its own independent MongoDB implementation of the same feature with no requestedBy, no fingerNumber check, and no sync to this one. See SEQ-04."
    note for FacialEmbedding "RN-28: only one active embedding per person at a time (isActive flag) — enroll() deactivates the previous template."
    note "All SQL classes also carry the standard audit block (created_at/updated_at/deleted_at/created_by/updated_by/deleted_by/row_version) — omitted here for readability. See AGENTS.md §2.2 and `06-data/domains/05-attendance.md` / `06-biometric.md` for the column-level ER view. The two MongoDB collections have no FKs by nature (cross-paradigm)."
